{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared vectors for where a labelled Divider puts its label and its two line segments.",
    "Read by coui_core (the closed form of the layout rule), coui_flutter (the rendered Divider)",
    "and a real-Chrome probe of the Web markup, so a change on one platform fails the other.",
    "All lengths are along the divider's main axis, in logical px on Flutter and CSS px on the Web.",
    "Positions are measured from the box's start edge in reading order: the left edge in ltr and",
    "the right edge in rtl for a horizontal divider, the top edge for a vertical one (a vertical",
    "divider ignores the text direction, so its cases hold in both).",
    "Inputs: box (the divider's own length), label (the child's own length), childPadding (the",
    "padding on each side of the child along the axis), indent and endIndent (the insets of the",
    "line at its start and its end), alignment (a CoreDividerChildAlignment name).",
    "Expected: labelCentre, the centre of the child; lines, the two painted segments in reading",
    "order as {start, end}, or null where the segment has no length; overflow, whether the child",
    "with its padding needs more than the box.",
    "directions, where a case states it, narrows the text directions the case holds in. A child",
    "wider than the box overflows: Flutter reports it, and its Row then anchors the children at",
    "the physical left edge in rtl as well as in ltr (nothing is left to distribute), where CSS",
    "anchors them at the start edge. So those cases are held in ltr only.",
    "intrinsic: rows for a horizontal divider whose parent takes its width from its content",
    "(Flutter IntrinsicWidth, CSS shrink-to-fit). There the box has no length of its own to share,",
    "so each weighted segment is as long as its inset allows the other to be: the box is the child",
    "with its padding plus the larger inset twice for the default alignment, and the child stays",
    "centred. width is the divider's own length."
  ],
  "directions": [
    "ltr",
    "rtl"
  ],
  "tolerance": {
    "flutter": 0.01,
    "web": 0.5
  },
  "crossExtent": 20,
